  "specification": {
    "unique_id": "typescript_api_gateway_expert_045",
    "name": "SocialPulse Gateway",
    "description": "SocialPulse Gateway is an expert-level, TypeScript-based API gateway designed for large-scale social platforms that aggregate diverse interaction streams\u2014posts, reactions, live chats, and stories\u2014into a single, coherent programmable surface. Sitting in front of a constellation of micro-services (timeline, media, messaging, notifications, and social-graph), it exposes both REST and GraphQL entry points while enforcing strict clean_architecture boundaries: presentation (controllers/resolvers), application (use-cases & DTOs), domain (aggregates, value objects, policies), and infrastructure (adapters & external integrations).\n\nThe gateway prioritizes social-centric concerns such as activity-feed fan-out, real-time presence, and community safety. Built-in rate-limiting and behavioral analytics guard against abusive patterns like follow-spam or message floods. Versioned routing enables gradual rollout of social algorithms (e.g., ranking V2) without breaking third-party clients. Response caching (Redis) accelerates high-fanout endpoints\u2014public timelines, trending hashtags\u2014while WebSocket subscriptions for GraphQL keep users up-to-date with new likes or comments. Comprehensive monitoring, structured logging, and OpenAPI/GraphQL self-documentation make the gateway production-ready for a rapidly evolving social ecosystem.",
